{"t": 1794115755.8074386, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Fixes #57.\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` computed the slice offset as `number * size`, which treats page numbers as 0-based. The API documents `?page=1` as the first page, so callers got the second page.\n\nChanged the offset to `(number - 1) * size`.\n\nChecked locally with a 10-item list and size 3:\n- page 1 -> [1, 2, 3]\n- page 2 -> [4, 5, 6]\n- page 4 -> [10]\n- page 5 -> []", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "fix(pager): treat page numbers as 1-based (#57)"}, "ok": true}
